WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.810
I'll take this guy instead for now!

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:06.900
If you wanna save this guy, you'll have to ask that card!

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:11.030
That will be the <i>key</i> that will allow us to meet again.

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:11.780
Yuma-<i>kun</i>!

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:12.860
Shingetsu!

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.300
Shingetsu!

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:19.060
Shingetsu! Shingetsu!

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:24.150
Shingetsu!

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:26.900
K-Kaito?!

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.620
Shingetsu!

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:29.050
Yuma.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.360
What's wrong? What happened?

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:36.280
Kaito! Shingetsu... was taken by Vector!

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:38.870
He was taken by a Barian!

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:44.080
I'm begging you...! I need your help searching for their location!

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.380
I'm begging you! Please!

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.260
Just calm down. It's unsightly.

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:53.260
Kaito...

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:03.190
Vector left this Number with us...

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:14.310
What is...?!

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:27.960
Some kind of map?

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:32.070
- Hey! Open up this instant, Yuma!
 - Hey!

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:32.720
Open up!

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:36.890
Gosh! That darn Yuma went and shunned us again!

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:38.180
Unforgivable!

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:41.100
If it's come to this, we need the flip side within the flip side, or not!

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:41.640
Huh?

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:55.030
So the one who kidnapped Shingetsu was the Barian who controlled Dr. Faker and Tron?

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:56.490
This guy called Vector?

00:01:56.490 --> 00:02:01.790
Yeah. I thought he was destroyed during that Duel back then.

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:06.290
<i>Damn you... bastards!</i>

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.000
I see.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:13.460
So he's shown himself before us again.

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:16.470
Isn't that amusing, Vector?!

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:19.340
I'll chase you down to the ends of this Earth!

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:22.060
But how do we find him?

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:25.020
We don't know anything about the Barians.

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:30.230
It doesn't matter! I owe that Vector bastard a good beating!

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.320
I swear to track him down and beat his ass!

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:35.320
You have such a simplistic way of thinking.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:37.360
What the hell did you say, you jerk?!

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:42.280
<i>K-Kaito-sama! It's terrible!</i>

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:46.960
<i>There's been a massive change
 in gravity right above us in this tower!</i>

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:48.960
Could it be the Barians?!

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:53.460
<i>It's just beginning now</i>

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:59.430
<i>This story continues to be etched into my heart endlessly</i>

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:02.140
<i>These feelings... burning up inside!</i>

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:14.490
<i>Preparations for the fight are ready</i>

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:17.570
<i>I can already hear the shivering of my heart</i>

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:22.080
<i>Been waiting this whole time</i>

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:24.450
<i>I may meet with defeat...</i>

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:27.670
<i>But that's exactly why I have to stand back up</i>

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:32.210
<i>Need to get stronger again</i>

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:34.340
<i>It's good to believe</i>

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:37.050
<i>The "now", more than ever before, is</i>

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.510
<i>but another limit to break down</i>

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:42.560
<i>I can cross with ease</i>

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:45.020
<i>It's just beginning now</i>

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:51.060
<i>This story continues to be etched into my heart endlessly</i>

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:53.820
<i>These feelings... burning up inside!</i>

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:55.280
<i>Right here in my hand,</i>

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:59.990
<i>I'm holding a powerful trump card.</i>

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:09.040
<i>With an unbreakable heart, I face toward my dream!</i>

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:30.490
"Let's Go to the Final Battle!
 Let's Start 'er up, the Emperor's Key Airship!!"

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.780
Wh-What the heck is that?!

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:06.210
Wh-What is this thing?!

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:09.580
This thing's from inside the Emperor's Key!

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:11.070
Why is it in the real world?

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:17.140
Astral! It was you?!

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:21.290
Yuma, I know where we must go now.

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:22.190
Wh-What?!

00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:26.890
After that Duel before, Vector left us with that Number.

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:30.810
That card is the key to activate this airship.

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:34.410
Furthermore, it came with the coordinates for their location.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:36.630
Their location? Where exactly are they?

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:40.090
Most likely in the Barian World.

00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:42.330
The Barian World?!

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:43.050
That's right.

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:48.010
Vector was calling us to this airship.

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:52.220
And there is a high possibility that your friend is there.

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:53.520
You mean Shingetsu?

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:56.520
Fine by me. Let's take it, then!

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:59.840
Wait. All of this sounds way too convenient.

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:01.650
Are you getting scared?

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:02.770
What?

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:05.200
If you're scared, you can stay and watch the house.

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:06.660
Knock it off already!

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:09.030
I'm going to save Shingetsu.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:13.340
And to do that, I'll be going alone!

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:15.830
All right.

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:19.210
The airship is currently filling with energy.

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:20.540
We will set sail tomorrow morning.

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:25.510
Yuma! Hey, Yuma!

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:28.890
Hey, what's that airship?

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:30.450
Do you know where Shingetsu-<i>kun</i> is?

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:35.560
Like I said, we need that airship to save Shingetsu!

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:40.070
L-Later, guys!

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:41.280
Hey!

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:43.400
Don't you run!

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:44.480
Wait!

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:45.400
Huh?

00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:49.060
Eh? Astral's airship?

00:06:49.150 --> 00:06:53.780
Yeah. That Barian called Vector is luring us.

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:54.580
Ryouga...

00:06:54.620 --> 00:07:01.120
He's the bastard that put you
 through all that and ruined our lives!

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.840
This time I'll beat him to a pulp!

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:06.170
For us?

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:08.530
You aren't honest with yourself.

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:10.180
What do you mean by that?

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:11.650
Well, that's fine.

00:07:11.650 --> 00:07:13.510
So, I'll be going with you.

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:16.180
Wh-Why would <i>you</i>...?

00:07:16.190 --> 00:07:17.370
Because I <i>decided</i> to.

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:21.850
And now that it's been decided,
 I'm hurrying off to go get ready.

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:26.860
Delicious!

00:07:29.180 --> 00:07:30.360
Darn good!

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:34.200
Today's Duel Supper is ridiculously good!

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:35.580
Idiot. Seconds.

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:37.540
Wh-What gives?

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:39.660
You're acting different than usual.

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:42.620
Grandma, thanks for everything!

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:45.170
Hey, Big Sis, you busy with work?

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:48.340
Whoa! What's gotten <i>into you</i> all of a sudden?

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:49.750
That's right, Big Sis!

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:52.070
I'll rub your shoulders!

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:53.280
H-Hey there!

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:55.710
Ah, I'll do yours after, Grandma.

00:07:57.950 --> 00:07:58.830
Shingetsu...

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:04.130
I'll use the cards you gave me, and I'll definitely...

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:08.300
Yuma.

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:09.720
Astral.

00:08:10.030 --> 00:08:14.910
I'm sure you already know this, but this fight is going to be fierce.

00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:17.660
Yeah, I know that.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:20.160
But I'm definitely gonna save Shingetsu!

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:24.370
So I can't afford to lose in these Duels!

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:29.840
Hey, Grandma, don't you think Yuma was acting strange?

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:32.550
Man, just what is he planning?

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:35.560
That boy is exactly like Kazuma.

00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:36.050
Huh?

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:39.720
Every time before he'd go off on some outrageous adventure,

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:43.440
Kazuma would always act that way.

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:46.810
Th-Then he...!
 I'm gonna go get him!

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:47.620
Don't bother.

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:48.360
But...!

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:54.320
All we can do is watch over that boy.

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:04.920
Brother.

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:12.090
Brother, you're going to fight against the Barians, aren't you?

00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:14.300
Yeah.

00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:17.460
I'm sorry you have to do this for me.

00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:19.730
No, that's not true.

00:09:19.730 --> 00:09:23.680
This battle is something I threw myself into.

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:26.980
It's all right. I won't lose.

00:09:26.990 --> 00:09:28.730
And I'll definitely return.

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:31.980
Okay. It's a promise, then.

00:09:45.260 --> 00:09:46.100
Yuma!

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:50.000
G-Guys...

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:51.930
Idiot. Forgot something.

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:56.470
D-Duel Lunch...

00:09:56.470 --> 00:09:58.180
Now go on.

00:09:58.180 --> 00:09:59.930
Idiot. Be careful.

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:02.260
Grandma... Obomi.

00:10:03.640 --> 00:10:07.190
You better be home by dinner.

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:08.060
Understand?

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:09.690
Sis!

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:12.820
Yeah! I'm off, then!

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:19.360
Sup! Everyone's early!

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:22.240
Tch, it's because of you.

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:23.330
Good morning.

00:10:23.330 --> 00:10:27.250
Hey, it's the Shark Sister! Why're you here?!

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:29.000
Do <i>not</i> call me Shark Sister!

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:32.500
I'll certainly be of some help to you.

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:34.880
Shark, is this okay with you?

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:36.840
She won't listen whether it is or isn't.

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:39.980
We got a bunch of fun friends together here!

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:43.760
Yuma, we're ready to ship off any time.

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:47.230
Heck yeah! Then let's get going!

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:49.940
But... how do we get on board?

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:55.110
This Flash Transformer will get us inside the cockpit.

00:10:56.280 --> 00:10:57.650
Wha...! What the?!

00:10:57.650 --> 00:10:59.760
Why are you guys here?!

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:01.500
That was cruel to leave us out, cat!

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:02.790
That's right!

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:05.630
Yuma! It's standoffish to not tell us anything, or not!

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:07.790
But I can't get you guys involved in this...

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:11.120
We also want to save Shingetsu!

00:11:11.130 --> 00:11:14.700
Shingetsu-<i>kun</i> is one of our precious friends!

00:11:15.710 --> 00:11:16.340
You guys...

00:11:17.750 --> 00:11:19.140
Then let's board.

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:32.060
Th-This is the cockpit?

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:37.870
A-Amazing!

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:45.080
I've confirmed our landing coordinates.

00:11:45.080 --> 00:11:48.410
This airship will now depart.

00:11:49.210 --> 00:11:52.410
We can all see Astral, or not!

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:53.120
Yeah!

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:56.090
So that's... Astral?

00:11:56.090 --> 00:12:00.630
Starting departure sequence. All systems online.

00:12:00.630 --> 00:12:02.040
Making contact with secondary systems!

00:12:04.810 --> 00:12:07.300
All systems confirmed to be working perfectly!

00:12:07.350 --> 00:12:10.680
Yuma, give us our instructions.

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:12.310
Huh? Me?

00:12:13.650 --> 00:12:17.110
I guess I'll allow you to take charge this time.

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:19.560
Just hurry up and do it!

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:20.860
Yuma, you can do it!

00:12:21.150 --> 00:12:23.320
All right, got it!

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:25.190
Departure preparations now complete!

00:12:26.290 --> 00:12:31.750
5, 4, 3, 2, 1...

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:32.750
Launch her!

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:33.950
Take off!

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:45.590
Wow! We're flying!

00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:49.560
Go on!

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:52.310
Opening the gate to the Different Dimensions.

00:12:56.560 --> 00:12:58.980
We are now breaking into the Different Dimension Space!

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:04.200
Now come to us!

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:07.950
Yuma Tsukumo! Astral!

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:13.580
We are now sailing smoothly toward our coordinated landmark.

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:15.620
So this is a Different Dimension tunnel!

00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:17.060
It's so quiet, or not!

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:18.540
That's for sure!

00:13:18.540 --> 00:13:21.500
But it's <i>too</i> quiet...

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:24.920
Oh yeah! I brought some beefsteaks!

00:13:26.510 --> 00:13:28.970
My grandma made a Duel Lunch for me!

00:13:28.970 --> 00:13:31.390
Yes! Let's all eat!

00:13:31.390 --> 00:13:33.730
God! Is this some <i>field trip</i>?

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:35.770
Grandma's Duel Lunch is...

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:42.530
What's up with these shocks?!

00:13:42.530 --> 00:13:46.280
I've confirmed several unidentified
 objects heading toward the airship!

00:13:47.140 --> 00:13:47.990
Those are...!

00:13:47.990 --> 00:13:49.030
Monsters?!

00:13:50.730 --> 00:13:52.450
They're left port bound in swarms!

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:54.750
Over here too!

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:55.690
They're here as well!

00:13:57.100 --> 00:13:58.990
Kaito! Shark! Let's go!

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:00.060
Me too!

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:01.220
I'm going too!

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:10.340
Come out, Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:14:12.670 --> 00:14:15.980
Come! Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon!

00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:19.570
Show yourself, Shark Drake!

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:23.630
Now come forth, Sylphine, the Sub-Zero Siren!

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:27.920
Come, Tinplate Archduke!

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:34.590
Go, Hope! Hope Sword Slash!

00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:40.880
Photon Stream of Destruction!

00:14:45.420 --> 00:14:46.720
Ice Ray!

00:14:54.470 --> 00:14:56.330
Heh! Didn't break a sweat!

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:57.260
It's strange...

00:14:57.260 --> 00:14:57.610
Huh?

00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:00.140
They're not putting up enough resistance.

00:15:00.140 --> 00:15:02.860
What is their aim here?

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:06.200
<i>Kaito-sama!</i>

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:06.900
What's wrong?!

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:11.160
It's terrible! A giant black hole has
 appeared in our ship's course!

00:15:12.350 --> 00:15:13.120
What did you say?!

00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:18.440
Yuma!

00:15:34.940 --> 00:15:36.260
Yuma.. Yuma...!

00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:38.270
Yuma! Yuma!

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:43.420
Are you okay, Yuma?

00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:44.860
Astral...

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:47.090
Where are we?

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:52.360
I'm not sure... but it doesn't appear to be the Barian World.

00:15:53.980 --> 00:15:55.330
Then we're...

00:15:55.330 --> 00:15:57.950
<i>But this place is...</i>

00:15:57.950 --> 00:15:59.580
Welcome to Sargasso!

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:05.540
I've been waiting for you, Yuma Tsukumo! And Astral!

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:07.320
You're Vector!

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:12.010
Did you have <i>fun</i> accepting
 the <i>greeting</i> my Monsters gave you?!

00:16:12.010 --> 00:16:14.300
So that really was you!

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:15.720
Where are we, Vector?!

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:18.770
It's the Different Dimension's Cemetery, Saragasso!

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:21.310
And it's the <i>last place</i> you fools will see!

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:25.560
Vector, Shingetsu...! Where's Shingetsu?!

00:16:27.470 --> 00:16:28.950
You wanna see him <i>that badly</i>?

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:32.570
Then I'll <i>let you see him</i>.

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:35.110
Your little friend, I mean!

00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:38.910
Shingetsu...!

00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:44.120
Hey, Shingetsu! Shingetsu!

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:47.880
Damn you, Vector! What'd you do to Shingetsu?!

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:54.800
So sorry, but your friend will never open his eyes <i>again</i>!

00:16:58.050 --> 00:17:02.090
Y-You're lying... No way... It's gotta be a lie!

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:09.730
Shingetsu...

00:17:11.070 --> 00:17:12.490
<i>Yuma Tsukumo-kun!</i>

00:17:12.490 --> 00:17:16.070
<i>Aren't you the champion of the W.D.C., Yuma Tsukumo-kun?</i>

00:17:16.070 --> 00:17:19.080
<i>I know I can't Duel well, but I'll give it my best shot!</i>

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:20.540
<i>Don't leave me out!</i>

00:17:20.830 --> 00:17:23.120
<i>Yes! It's for the best!</i>

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:27.790
Shingetsu!!

00:17:30.590 --> 00:17:34.050
Th-This can't be...! Shingetsu-<i>kun</i>...!

00:17:38.010 --> 00:17:39.140
Yuma...

00:17:39.510 --> 00:17:41.600
So you're Ryouga Kamishiro?

00:17:43.070 --> 00:17:44.430
Who the hell are <i>you</i>?!

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:49.650
My name is Durbe. And you shall be defeated by me in a Duel.

00:17:49.650 --> 00:17:53.110
Oh? So you're the first Barian I get to <i>slaughter</i>?

00:17:53.110 --> 00:17:55.990
I'll be sure to <i>engrave your name</i> in my mind.

00:18:00.490 --> 00:18:03.950
It's been some time, Kaito.

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:06.120
Misael...

00:18:08.470 --> 00:18:13.460
Today we'll make it clear who the <i>true</i> Galaxy-Eyes user is!

00:18:14.170 --> 00:18:17.630
That's just what I wanted, Misael!

00:18:17.630 --> 00:18:21.220
<i>C'mon</i>! Don't be so <i>sad</i>!

00:18:21.230 --> 00:18:24.060
You guys'll be seeing him <i>really soon</i>!

00:18:24.060 --> 00:18:28.560
And that's because you won't be leaving this place <i>alive</i>!

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:30.330
Unforgivable...

00:18:32.190 --> 00:18:35.490
I'll <i>never</i> forgive you, Vector!

00:18:35.930 --> 00:18:38.200
I swear I'm gonna beat the hell out of you!

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:40.530
Here goes!

00:18:42.840 --> 00:18:44.850
Duel Disk, set!

00:19:10.090 --> 00:19:12.250
D-Gazer, set!

00:19:13.770 --> 00:19:14.730
Duel!!

00:19:15.940 --> 00:19:16.690
Duel!!

00:19:19.150 --> 00:19:20.740
Duel!!

00:19:25.490 --> 00:19:27.500
Yuma...

00:19:27.790 --> 00:19:30.590
My turn! Draw!

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:34.090
I Summon Goblindbergh!

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:36.770
When this card is Summoned successfully,

00:19:37.170 --> 00:19:41.320
I can Special Summon one
 Level Four or lower Monster from my hand!

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:44.620
Come on, Ganbara Knight!

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:50.850
I Overlay the Level Four Goblindbergh and Ganbara Knight!

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:56.940
I use these two Monsters to build the Overlay Network!

00:19:57.640 --> 00:19:58.730
Xyz Summon!

00:20:00.770 --> 00:20:05.230
Come out, Number 39! Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:20:08.620 --> 00:20:13.620
Oh? You sure aren't very well <i>composed</i> if you're Summoning your Ace right off the bat, <i>hmm</i>?!

00:20:13.620 --> 00:20:14.830
Damn you!

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:16.160
Yuma!

00:20:16.160 --> 00:20:18.050
I know how you feel, but you need to calm down!

00:20:19.520 --> 00:20:21.970
I Summon Double-Fin Shark!

00:20:26.070 --> 00:20:29.140
Then, because I have a Water-Attribute Monster on my field,

00:20:29.470 --> 00:20:32.350
I can Special Summon Silent Angler!

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:36.060
And when Double-Fin Shark is used as Xyz Material,

00:20:36.480 --> 00:20:38.230
it can be treated as two!

00:20:38.700 --> 00:20:43.030
I Overlay the Level Four Double-Fin Shark and Silent Angler!

00:20:44.920 --> 00:20:46.220
Xyz Summon!

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:54.290
Roar, Number 32!
 Marine Biting Dragon - Shark Drake!

00:20:59.380 --> 00:21:01.840
I Special Summon Photon Slasher!

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:06.250
This card can be Special Summoned
 when I have no Monsters on my field!

00:21:06.730 --> 00:21:09.110
Then I Summon Photon Delta Wing!

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:18.340
I Overlay the Level Four Photon Slasher and Photon Delta Wing!

00:21:21.290 --> 00:21:22.420
Xyz Summon!

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:27.780
Show yourself, Radiant Light Emperor Galaxion!

00:21:30.660 --> 00:21:32.660
Kaito...

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:34.670
You fool!

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:39.120
I activate the effect of the Field Magic,
 Ancient Battlefield of the Different Dimension - Sargasso!

00:21:39.370 --> 00:21:39.970
What?!

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:52.960
Yuma!

00:22:00.230 --> 00:22:01.530
What <i>is</i> this...?!

00:22:01.530 --> 00:22:03.900
Could this field be...?!

00:22:17.370 --> 00:22:24.250
<i>Does the thought "In any case..." following</i>

00:22:24.660 --> 00:22:31.920
<i>the foreboding premonition tell you to give up?</i>

00:22:31.920 --> 00:22:39.510
<i>Do you laugh at your dreams, saying "impossible"?</i>

00:22:39.510 --> 00:22:46.850
<i>You must find it funny that I'm not able to laugh at it, right?</i>

00:22:47.400 --> 00:23:03.790
<i>This song supports me, so I'll do my best for you this time.
 It's my turn to sing now.</i>

00:23:03.790 --> 00:23:08.580
<i>I will vow to you here</i>

00:23:08.580 --> 00:23:18.930
<i>As long as I live, you'll always be my tiny, little friend</i>

00:23:18.930 --> 00:23:27.480
<i>I'll erase all those little mistakes of yours</i>

00:23:27.480 --> 00:23:32.270
<i>Because I want to become an artist</i>

00:23:34.070 --> 00:23:38.570
<i>Look, I like doing it 'cuz it's fun.</i>

00:23:40.390 --> 00:23:42.770
Our battle against the Barians has finally begun!

00:23:43.510 --> 00:23:44.860
We've fallen for Vector's clever trap!

00:23:45.240 --> 00:23:46.430
His fangs are untouchable!

00:23:46.820 --> 00:23:48.440
The Over-Hundred Number!

00:23:49.220 --> 00:23:52.010
And he reveals to us a shocking truth!

00:23:52.180 --> 00:23:54.140
I will get revenge for Shingetsu!

00:23:54.140 --> 00:23:55.700
It's strange... This Duel...

00:23:55.950 --> 00:23:57.650
No way! Then Yuma...

00:23:57.980 --> 00:23:59.980
The Full-Powered Hope Ray V!

00:24:00.980 --> 00:24:02.140
Deck Destruction!?

00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:04.170
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal II!

00:24:04.410 --> 00:24:07.000
"Vector's Madness: 
The Battle Aboard the Ominous Sargasso!"

00:24:07.400 --> 00:24:09.610
Just who the hell <i>are</i> you?!
